UPDATE companies SET description='Green Gables Furniture traces its roots to Bradford, Illinois, where a family-owned operation began building furniture out of a three-car garage in the 1980s. The company remains family owned today, carrying forward the same work ethic and commitment to craftsmanship that defined its early days.

Today the company produces solid wood furniture entirely in the United States, working with reclaimed barnwood, live-edge hardwoods such as walnut, cherry, hickory, and white oak, and incorporating steel elements. Each piece is handcrafted, emphasizing natural grain, knots, saw marks, and the character of the materials. Collections range from rustic Western styles to clean contemporary designs, all built to highlight the authenticity of the wood.

Green Gables serves the residential furniture market, supplying both retail dealers and end consumers who furnish homes with its collections.

The company says its differentiation lies in blending traditional woodworking techniques with fresh design ideas, using reclaimed timbers and live edges to create furniture that gains character over time. The goal, unchanged since the garage days, is to build honest, durable pieces meant to be passed down through generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solid wood furniture manufacturing", "Reclaimed wood processing", "Live-edge woodworking", "Metal-wood fabrication", "Handcrafted finishing", "Custom furniture design"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings", "Interior design", "Furniture retail"], "materials": ["Solid wood", "Reclaimed barnwood", "Walnut", "Cherry", "Hickory", "White Oak", "Steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since the 1980s", "Solid wood furniture made in the USA", "Use of reclaimed barnwood and live-edge hardwoods", "Combination of traditional woodworking with steel accents", "Designed to last for generations"], "facts_used": ["Family-owned operation started in 1980s in a three-car garage -> /about-us", "Located in Bradford, Illinois -> db", "Produces solid wood furniture using reclaimed barnwood, live-edge hardwoods (walnut, cherry, hickory, white oak) and steel -> /about-us", "Sells through dealer network and direct to consumers -> /about-us", "Focus on handcrafted, durable furniture designed to last generations -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Green Gables Furniture has always been about more than building furniture. It''s about building something that lasts. Our story began in the 1980s, when a family-owned operation started building furniture out of a three-car garage.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='green-gables-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Green Leaf Solar operates from Columbia, Missouri. The company is owned by Ryan Roe, who brings a mathematics background to system design. The founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The firm provides turnkey solar photovoltaic installations for homes and businesses. Its services include identifying all available incentives, rebates, and financing options to minimize payback periods, sometimes with zero money down. The installation team, led by chief troubleshooter Martin Podolak and solar technicians Alex and Carlos, backs each project with a 10‑ to 30‑year parts warranty, a 10‑year "Done Right" installation guarantee, and a five‑year labor warranty on part failure. Sales manager Jay Hasheider, a former utility renewable‑energy specialist with over three decades of experience, supports customer acquisition and education.

Green Leaf Solar serves residential and commercial customers in the Columbia area. Its client base includes homeowners seeking to reduce electricity bills and businesses aiming to hedge against rising energy costs. The company emphasizes a low‑risk approach, handling incentive paperwork and system design so that customers can adopt solar without upfront capital.

The company states that its differentiation lies in eliminating risk for the property owner, securing the shortest possible payback through exhaustive incentive research, and standing behind installations with long‑term warranties and a dedicated service team. Its approach is built on reliability, dependable pricing, and exceptional service, as outlined by the ownership team.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system installation", "Incentive, rebate, and loan identification", "System design and optimization", "Maintenance and troubleshooting"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Finds all incentives, rebates, and loans for shortest payback time", "Zero money down options available", "10\u2011 to 30\u2011year parts warranty", "10\u2011year \"Done Right\" installation guarantee", "5\u2011year labor warranty on part failure"], "facts_used": ["Location: Columbia, Missouri -> db", "Owner: Ryan Roe -> /about", "Team members: Jay Hasheider, Martin Podolak, Alex, Carlos -> /about", "Services: incentive/rebate/loan identification, solar PV installation -> /", "Warranties: 10-30 year parts, 10-year installation guarantee, 5-year labor -> /", "Customer types: homes and businesses -> /", "Differentiators: risk elimination, zero money down, shortest payback -> /", "Company focus: reliability, dependability, fair prices, exceptional service -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Green Leaf Solar specializes in finding all incentives, rebates and loans available. ... We give a 10 year \"Done Right\" Guaranty on all Installs.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='green-leaf-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Green Mountain Semiconductor, Inc. was founded in 2015 by three colleagues in Burlington, Vermont. The company began as a collaborative project among friends and evolved into a professional design organization focused on semiconductor solutions.

The firm provides custom analog, digital, and mixed-signal design services, with deep expertise in memory design including DRAM, SRAM, and emerging non-volatile memories. It offers a full flow from early technology development through test chips and test programs, specializing in compute-in-memory architectures, neuromorphic processors, and high-speed PHY interfaces such as LPDDR4/4X/5 and SPI/QPI. All design work is performed by its own employees at its Burlington office, and the team has experience in advanced nodes including 7 nm TSMC.

Green Mountain serves aerospace and defense, medical devices, and high-performance computing markets. In aerospace, it develops radiation-hardened chips that process sensor data in situ at low power. For medical devices, it creates low-power integrated circuits for patient monitoring and diagnosis, including neuromorphic edge-computing IP. The company has executed development contracts with the National Science Foundation and NASA, the latter for a family of rad-hard neuromorphic processors.

The company differentiates itself through its patented technology in commodity memory architecture, error correction, and in-memory high-parallel data processing, holding seven patents in compute-in-memory. It emphasizes a one-stop-shop approach for implementing complex algorithms into proven silicon, and maintains CMMC 2.0 certification.', certifications=ARRAY['CMMC 2.0']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom ASIC design", "Analog & mixed-signal design", "Digital design", "Memory design (DRAM, SRAM, emerging NVM)", "Compute-in-memory architecture", "Neuromorphic processor design", "Radiation-hardened design", "High-speed PHY design (LPDDR4/4X/5, SPI/QPI)", "Low-power design", "AI circuit design / in-memory computing", "Full custom development (from technology development to test chips)", "Special purpose application development", "Interface solutions", "Emerging memory development", "Patent development"], "industries": ["Aerospace and Defense", "Medical Devices", "High-Performance Computing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% US-based design team in Burlington, VT", "Seven patents in compute-in-memory and memory architecture", "Deep expertise in DRAM, SRAM, and emerging NVM design", "Experience with advanced process nodes including 7 nm TSMC", "CMMC 2.0 certified"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2015 -> db", "Headquartered in Burlington, Vermont -> db and homepage (/) mentions ''offices in Burlington, VT''", "Started as project of three friends and colleagues -> homepage (/) ''Our story started as the project of three friends and colleagues''", "Specializes in custom analog, digital & mixed-signal design -> homepage (/) ''GMS specializes in Custom Analog, Digital & Mixed Signal design''", "Deep roots in memory design (DRAM, SRAM, emerging NVM) -> homepage (/) ''deep roots in Memory Design (DRAM, SRAM, Emerging NVM)''", "7 patents on compute-in-memory architectures -> homepage (/) ''filed 7 patents so far on this topic''", "Developing rad-hard neuromorphic processors for NASA -> homepage (/) ''currently sponsored by this agency for designing a family of rad-hard neuromorphic processors''", "CMMC 2.0 certification achieved March 2026 -> homepage (/) ''CMMC 2.0 certification achieved''", "Member of National Semiconductor Technology Center (NSTC) -> homepage (/) ''becomes a member of the National Semiconductor Technology Center (NSTC)''", "100% US based, designs performed by employees in Burlington, VT -> homepage (/) ''Green Mountain Semiconductor is 100% US based. All of our designs are performed by our own employees at our offices in Burlington, VT''", "Experience with 7nm TSMC process -> homepage (/) ''track record in advanced technology nodes such as 7nm TSMC''", "High speed PHY interfaces: LPDDR4/4X/5, SPI/QPI -> homepage (/) ''developed a family of secondary LPDDR4/4X/5 PHY as well as SPI/QPI''", "Serves aerospace and defense, medical devices, high-performance computing -> homepage (/) ''Markets: Aerospace and Defense, High-Performance Computing, Medical Devices''"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a design services firm specializing in cutting-edge semiconductor solutions.", "founded_year": "2015", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='green-mountain-semiconductor-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Green Mountain Solar was founded in 2017 in South Burlington, Vermont. The company operates from its headquarters in South Burlington and maintains a second office in East Dorset to serve customers across the state. No specific ownership structure or founders are disclosed in public materials.

The firm provides full-service solar design, project management, and installation for residential and commercial clients. Its offerings include photovoltaic panel arrays, battery backup systems, heat pump installations, and electric vehicle charger setups. An in-house service team handles post-installation maintenance and support.

Green Mountain Solar serves homeowners and businesses throughout Vermont. Its customer base includes individuals seeking to reduce electricity costs and carbon footprint, as well as commercial property owners adding renewable energy infrastructure. The company also works with utility programs such as Green Mountain Power’s leased battery offerings.

