UPDATE companies SET description='H3 Plastics LLC is a family-owned rigid packaging manufacturer based in American Fork, Utah. The company launched in 2020 during the height of the COVID-19 bottle shortage, when an urgent need for packaging created a business culture centered on speed, quality, and responsive customer service. Although young, the business draws on decades of experience in manufacturing, construction, and engineering from its founders, instilling a culture of hard work, reliability, and long-term partnerships.

H3 produces both stock and custom plastic containers using Injection Stretch Blow Molding (ISBM), Reheat Blow Molding (RHB), and Injection Blow Molding processes. The facility runs modern blow molding platforms suited for small to mid-sized volume programs, working primarily with PET, HDPE, and post-consumer recycled (PCR) blends. In-house capabilities include design engineering, tooling management, finite element analysis, 3D prototyping, and integrated quality inspections covering gram weight, neck finishes, wall thickness, and leak testing. For hot-fill applications, the company offers MOQ flexibility down to 25,000 units.

The company serves health and nutrition, food and beverage, personal care, cosmetic, pet care, and household chemical markets. Customers range from medtech and specialty food brands to personal care companies, all supported by a dedicated design team and assigned representatives.

H3 differentiates itself through its family-owned values—hard work, reliability, quality control, and pride—and through certified quality systems (SQF and IMS). Sustainability is engineered into operations via lightweight designs, PCR material options, reusable packaging solutions, and energy-efficient auxiliary systems.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF-certified','IMS-certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Stretch Blow Molding (ISBM)", "Reheat Blow Molding (RHB)", "Injection Blow Molding", "Custom packaging design", "In-house tooling management", "Finite element analysis (FEA)", "3D in-house prototyping", "Quality inspections (gram weight, neck finishes, wall thickness, leak testing)", "Hot fill PET container production", "PCR blend material processing", "Lightweight packaging design", "Reusable packaging solutions", "Preventative maintenance programs", "AQL inspection methods", "Material compliance and regulatory support"], "industries": ["Health and nutrition", "Food and beverage", "Personal care", "Cosmetic", "Pet care", "Household chemical"], "materials": ["PET", "HDPE", "PCR blends"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Small to mid-volume programs; MOQ 25,000 units for hot fill projects", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, flexible, responsive culture", "SQF and IMS certified quality systems", "In-house design, tooling, and finite element analysis", "Hot-fill PET capabilities on ISBM and RHB platforms with 25,000-unit MOQ", "Sustainability focus: PCR blends, lightweighting, reusable packaging"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2020 during COVID-19 bottle shortage -> /about", "Family-owned -> /about", "Headquarters in American Fork, Utah -> db", "Processes: Injection Stretch Blow Molding, Reheat Blow Molding, Injection Blow Molding -> /capabilities", "Industries served: health and nutrition, food & beverage, personal care, cosmetic, pet care, household chemical -> /", "Certifications: SQF-certified, IMS-certified -> /capabilities"