UPDATE companies SET description='HMB Electronics operates from North Haven, Connecticut, as a women-owned small business. The company was established to meet growing demand for expedited shipments of electronic components, leveraging a vast network of suppliers both domestically and internationally to serve customers across the Northeast and beyond.

As a stocking distributor, HMB Electronics carries a broad line of name-brand electronic components including integrated circuits, resistors, transistors, capacitors, connectors, and computer peripherals. The firm maintains a fully equipped warehouse with temperature control, anti-static workbenches, and full-time monitoring to ensure proper handling of sensitive parts. Core services encompass same-day shipping on stocked items, obsolete and end-of-life component sourcing, cross-referencing for alternative parts, excess inventory purchasing, and third-party component testing and verification through a regional facility.

The company serves government agencies, original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), contract manufacturers (CMs), and both franchised and non-franchised distributors. Its customer base spans military, information technology, and general OEM sectors, with components sourced from manufacturers such as Analog Devices, Texas Instruments, Intel, Xilinx, Maxim, and numerous other brands.

HMB Electronics differentiates itself through a 110% quality guarantee, AS5553 compliance for counterfeit electronic parts avoidance, and a commitment to providing manufacturer traceability certificates wherever possible. The firm’s partnership with an independent testing facility and its excess inventory purchasing program further reinforce its focus on authenticity and supply-chain reliability.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','AS5553']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Obsolete and EOL component sourcing", "Cross-referencing and alternative part identification", "Excess inventory purchasing", "Component testing and verification", "Same-day shipping", "Manufacturer traceability documentation"], "industries": ["Government", "OEM", "Contract Manufacturer", "Franchised distributors", "Non-franchised distributors", "Military", "Information Technology"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping on stocked items; next-day expedited shipping available", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on stocked items", "AS5553 compliance for counterfeit electronic parts avoidance", "Third-party component testing and verification", "Manufacturer traceability certificates provided", "Excess inventory purchasing to expand stock"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: North Haven, CT -> /about", "Women-Owned Small Business -> /about", "Stocking distributor of name-brand electronic components -> /", "Same-day shipping and expedited next-day shipping -> /", "Obsolete/EOL sourcing, cross-references, excess inventory purchasing, testing -> /services", "Industries served: government, OEM, CM, franchised/non-franchised distributors -> /", "Component brands: Analog Devices, TI, Intel, Xilinx, Maxim, etc. -> /", "Warehouse with temperature control, anti-static workbenches, monitoring -> /about", "AS5553 compliance certificate -> products array", "ISO9001 certification -> certifications array", "LinkedIn URL -> linkedin_url"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "HMB Electronics is a stocking distributor of name brand electronic components with discount pricing and same day shipments.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/hmb-electronics/"], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hmb-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Haake Manufacturing Co. was founded in 1948 by Fred C. Haake Sr. and his wife Elfriede in a St. Louis garage as a small tool-and-die shop. The German-trained machinist started with a single punch press and a commitment to quality that quickly earned the trust of local manufacturers. In 1963, the second generation—Fred Jr. and Lorraine Haake—relocated the operation to De Soto, Missouri, adding a company-owned trucking fleet to guarantee on-time delivery. Today, the fourth-generation family business is led by Jay Rieker and operates from a 100,000-square-foot facility in De Soto.

The company provides precision custom sheet metal fabrication entirely under one roof. Core processes include CNC laser cutting (up to 10,000 watts), CNC punching, combined punch/laser processing, CNC press brake forming with six-axis back gauges, metal stamping using AIDA cells up to 160 tons and auxiliary presses from 5 to 150 tons, robotic MIG/MAG welding of steel, stainless steel, and aluminum, and a fully automated powder coating line with six-stage wash, infrared pre-processing, and zirconium pretreatment. Secondary services such as assembly, hardware insertion, and metal finishing coordination deliver turnkey components.

Haake serves manufacturers across the United States from its central U.S. location, with a historical customer base that includes aerospace firms such as McDonnell Douglas and a broad range of Midwest industrial companies. The shop handles short-run prototypes through long-run production volumes, emphasizing just-in-time delivery programs that support inventory management and cash flow.

The company differentiates itself through integrated, in-house capabilities that eliminate supplier handoffs, a central location enabling two-day shipping to either coast, ISO 9001:2015 certification with reported defect rates of 292 PPM for fabrication and 0 PPM for powder coating, and a 99% on-time delivery record. Low operating costs powered partly by solar energy and a domestic supply chain focus further support cost competitiveness and reshoring efforts.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC Laser Cutting", "CNC Punching", "CNC Punch/Laser Combination", "CNC Press Brake Forming", "Metal Stamping", "Robotic MIG/MAG Welding", "Powder Coating", "Assembly", "Hardware Insertion", "Metal Finishing Coordination"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "General Manufacturing", "Industrial Manufacturing"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless Steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Trumpf CNC Systems", "Fiber Lasers", "10,000 Watt Laser", "AIDA Punching Cells (up to 160 tons)", "Presses (5 to 150 tons)", "Robotic Welding Cells", "Automated Powder Coating Line (six-stage wash, infrared pre-processing, zirconium pretreatment)", "Electric Press Brakes with Six-Axis Back Gauges"], "volume": "Short to long runs; medium to high volume production", "lead_time": "Two-day shipping to either coast; quick turnaround", "tolerances": "Tight tolerances (specific values not stated)", "built_on": ["Two-day shipping to either coast from central U.S. location", "ISO 9001:2015 certified with 292 PPM fabrication defect rate and 0 PPM powder coating defect rate (2025)", "99% on-time delivery with just-in-time inventory programs", "All fabrication, finishing, and assembly capabilities under one roof", "One of few St. Louis region job shops with combined punch/laser processing on a single machine"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1948 by Fred C. Haake Sr. and Elfriede in St. Louis garage -> /about", "Relocated to De Soto, Missouri in 1963 by second generation -> /about", "F