UPDATE companies SET description='Hampshire Controls Corporation was established in 1976 in Dover, New Hampshire, where it remains headquartered. The company began as a designer and manufacturer of monitoring, logging, and alert status notification systems, emphasizing "Made in the USA" reliability for demanding applications.

The firm designs and produces a range of NIST-traceable calibrated instruments, including temperature monitors and alarms for blood and plasma, cryogenic temperature monitors, multi-probe condition monitors, data logging and alarm systems, Wi-Fi temperature transmitters, biomedical freezer backup systems (liquid CO2 and liquid nitrogen), liquid nitrogen level monitors, and laboratory air flow monitors. Engineering, manufacturing, testing, and calibration are performed in-house at the Dover facility, covering PCB soldering, cable manufacturing, subsystem interfacing, final electronic assembly, firmware development, and custom enclosure design.

Hampshire Controls serves blood banks, vaccine and genetic research laboratories, biopharma production facilities, governmental agencies, hospitals, commercial food processing and storage operations, and industrial manufacturing firms. The company works directly with original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), government agencies, research laboratories, and industrial customers, supplying both standard and custom-engineered products for applications such as blood product verification, cryogenic storage monitoring, and environmental condition logging.

The company differentiates itself through its U.S.-based design and manufacturing, NIST-traceable calibration services, and the ability to deliver fully custom systems — from mechanical and electrical engineering through firmware, testing, and calibration — under one roof. Its products carry UL Listing, and the firm holds a U.S. government CAGE code (0H2P8) for federal procurement.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom engineering and manufacturing services", "Customization of standard monitoring and alarm systems", "Mechanical engineering (enclosure design, NEMA/IP ratings)", "Electrical engineering (analog, digital, mixed-signal PCB design)", "Firmware development (application-specific, communication protocols)", "PCB soldering and assembly", "Cable manufacturing", "Subsystem interfacing", "Final electronic product assembly", "Electronic testing and burn-in", "NIST-traceable calibration", "Private labeling and custom panel design", "Wireless connectivity integration (RF, Wi-Fi, Cellular LTE)", "Ethernet and Wi-Fi network integration", "Communication protocol implementation (BACnet, Modbus, MQTT, HTTP/HTTPS)", "Sensor data acquisition, amplification, and filtering", "Power supply design (line-powered, battery-powered, low-power)", "Microcontroller selection and optimization", "Condition monitoring (temperature, humidity, pressure, gas concentration, liquid level)", "Liquid nitrogen (LN2) and CO2 freezer backup system design", "Air flow monitoring system design"], "industries": ["Blood banks", "Cryogenic biologic storage", "Vaccine research laboratories", "Genetic research laboratories", "Biopharma production facilities", "Government agencies", "Hospitals", "Commercial food processing and storage", "Industrial manufacturing", "Clinical", "Food and beverage", "Water distribution and plumbing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["MPS series multi-probe monitors/alarms", "TT-150 & TT-200 Battery Operated Wi-Fi Temperature Transmit