UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 2010 in Baton Rouge, Louisiana, Hanley''s Foods began as a salad-loving venture by Richard and Kate Hanley, who launched their first dressing at the Red Stick Farmer''s Market in 2012 after discovering their favorite restaurant-style dressing was unavailable in stores. The couple, together since high school, refined their recipe through family taste tests before partnering with the LSU AgCenter''s Food Incubator to bring the product to market.

The company produces premium, all-natural salad dressings and croutons from scratch at its Louisiana facility, using locally sourced ingredients. Hanley''s focuses exclusively on these two product lines, manufacturing every bottle in-house. Today its products are stocked in more than 2,000 retail locations across the United States, including major chains such as Walmart, Costco, Whole Foods, and regional grocers like Rouses Markets.

Hanley''s serves the retail grocery sector and foodservice operators, with customers ranging from national big-box retailers to hospitality groups such as Compass Group and Royal Caribbean. The company also offers wholesale partnerships for independent grocers and specialty stores.

The founders say their differentiation lies in a single-minded commitment to quality: premium natural ingredients, Louisiana-made production, and adherence to rigorous food-safety standards including HACCP, NSF, SQF, GMP, and supporting programs such as SOP, SSOP, CCP, and CAP.', certifications=ARRAY['HACCP','GMP','SQF','NSF','SOP','SSOP','CCP','CAP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Salad dressing manufacturing", "Crouton manufacturing"], "industries": ["Retail", "Foodservice"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-focus on premium salad dressings and croutons", "All products made from scratch in Louisiana", "Premium natural locally-sourced ingredients", "Certified to HACCP, NSF, SQF, GMP and supporting food-safety programs", "Distributed in over 2,000 retail stores nationwide"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2010 in Baton Rouge, Louisiana -> db", "Founders Richard and Kate Hanley -> /about", "Originated 2012 at Red Stick Farmer''s Market -> /about", "Partnered with LSU AgCenter Food Incubator -> /about", "Products: premium natural salad dressings and croutons -> /about", "Made from scratch in Louisiana -> /about", "Over 2,000 retail stores across US -> /about", "Retail customers: Walmart, Costco, Whole Foods, Compass Group, Royal Caribbean, Rouses Markets, AG Stores -> /about", "Certifications: HACCP, GMP, SQF, NSF, SOP, SSOP, CCP, CAP -> /about", "Company type: Manufacturer -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We do one thing and one thing only, make damn-good dressings & croutons using premium, natural, locally-sourced ingredients in south Louisiana.", "founded_year": "2010", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hanley-s-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Hansen Advertising, Inc. has operated from Willmar, Minnesota since its founding in 1962. The company remains family owned and operated, now in its third generation of ownership. The business began as a promotional products supplier and has maintained a focus on personal relationships as its guiding principle.

The firm sources and customizes a full line of promotional products, sportswear, and business apparel for clients ranging from schools and churches to corporations. An in-house graphic artist assists with logo creation and artwork preparation, while a physical showroom allows customers to examine samples before ordering. Sales representatives attend industry trade shows and seminars to stay current on product trends and can deliver or mail samples directly to clients.

Hansen serves a broad base of organizations, including educational institutions, religious groups, general businesses, and event planners. The company has developed programs for meetings, conferences, product launches, sports events, and employee or volunteer appreciation. Recent blog content highlights specialized offerings for casino nights, wedding favors, and team recognition awards.

