UPDATE companies SET description='Heisler Semiconductor operates a process and assembly lab in Halethorpe, Maryland. The company is a US-based, engineering-led advanced packaging team; no founding year or individual founders are disclosed in public materials.

The lab provides advanced packaging and wafer-level services including die attach, wire bonding, flip chip, hermetic sealing, and 3D integration; wafer-level processing such as lithography, TSV, deposition, etch, CMP, and RDL; laser micromachining for micro-vias, dicing, singulation, and marking; and inspection and metrology via X-ray, 3D AOI, SEM, and sub-micron metrology. The same engineering team also handles circuit, device, and hardware design, firmware development, RF evaluation boards, and domestic supply-chain management from prototype through qualified volume.

Heisler serves aerospace and defense, medical and bio, RF/mmWave, and advanced sensor programs where domestic provenance and high-reliability assembly are required. Customers include companies building MEMS, sensors, GaN and CMOS mixed-signal devices, and fine-pitch multi-die modules.

The company emphasizes a data-driven, AI-native approach: designed experiments (DOE) and statistical process control on every build, with AI surfacing drift and correlations to reduce trial-and-error iterations. All development and build work remains on US soil under an NDA-first policy, and the engineers who scope a job own it through qualification.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL-STD']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Die attach", "Wire bonding", "Flip chip", "Hermetic sealing", "3D integration", "Wafer-level lithography", "Through-silicon via (TSV) formation", "Thin-film deposition", "Etch", "Chemical mechanical planarization (CMP)", "Redistribution layer (RDL) fabrication", "Laser micromachining (micro-vias, dicing, singulation, marking)", "X-ray inspection", "3D automated optical inspection (AOI)", "Scanning electron microscopy (SEM)", "Sub-micron metrology", "Cross-section failure analysis", "Circuit design", "Device design", "Hardware design", "Firmware development", "RF evaluation board design", "Domestic supply chain management", "Turnkey assembly"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Medical & Bio", "RF/mmWave", "Advanced Sensors"], "materials": ["Silicon", "Sapphire", "Aluminum nitride (AlN)", "Polyimide", "Underfills", "Thin-film materials"], "equipment": ["BESI Datacon die bonding/flip chip platform", "Tresky precision die attach platform", "Keyence microscopy and metrology", "Creative Electron X-ray inspection", "UV 355nm laser micromachining", "IR 1064nm laser micromachining"], "volume": "Prototype to qualified volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Placement \u00b12.5 \u00b5m at 3\u03c3 on BESI Datacon and Tresky platforms", "built_on": ["One engineering team owns the program from design review through qualified volume", "DOE-driven process development with SPC and aggregated build data", "AI-assisted iteration reduction using shop-floor metrology and test data", "All development and production performed on US soil with a domestic supply chain"