The company’s core offering includes industrial switchgear, power distribution equipment, and electrical control systems. It employs between 50 and 99 people and targets commercial, industrial, and institutional clients. Information about facility square footage, annual volumes, or catalog depth is not disclosed.

Its customer base spans the industrial, commercial, and institutional sectors. Typical applications involve power distribution and switchgear for manufacturing facilities, commercial buildings, and campus-style institutions such as hospitals or universities.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": [], "industries": ["Industrial", "Commercial", "Institutional"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1972 -> db", "Headquartered in Hawthorne, New York -> db", "Employee count 50-99 -> db", "Products: Industrial Switchgear, Power Distribution Equipment -> db", "Industries served: Industrial, Commercial -> db", "Description: supplier of industrial switchgear and power distribution equipment -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "supplier of industrial switchgear and power distribution equipment", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "50-99", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hudson-electric-sales-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Huetter Mill & Cabinet operates from Murray, Utah, where it was founded in 1948 by German immigrant Alfred Huetter. It remains a family-owned company, now led by President Gordon Huetter, Alfred’s son.

The company provides full-service custom millwork, including hardwood moldings stocked in alder, knotty alder, maple, poplar, cherry, and oak, as well as stair parts, handrails, and complete stairway systems. Its manufacturing facility produces custom cabinetry for large commercial and high-end residential projects, supported by an extensive inventory of custom knives for unique profiles. The firm maintains over $1.2 million in inventory on hand and ships nationally from its Utah location.

Huetter serves commercial construction, residential new construction, and remodeling markets, with a specialty in historic renovations. Notable projects include the Utah Governor’s Mansion, the Utah State Capitol, The Children’s Center, and O.C. Tanner renovations.

The company’s stated purpose is to provide a financially sound operation for wholesale millwork and commercial shop products at reasonable cost, delivered efficiently by trained craftsmen. Its motto, “Quality and Craftsmanship live in our Name,” reflects an emphasis on material selection, advanced machinery, and skilled workmanship as differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom millwork", "Stair parts manufacturing", "Hardwood molding production", "Custom cabinetry", "Historic renovation millwork", "Custom knife/profile creation", "Stairway installation", "Wholesale millwork distribution"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Residential construction", "Remodeling", "Historic restoration", "Education", "Healthcare", "Government", "Tenant improvements"], "materials": ["Alder", "Knotty Alder", "Maple", "Poplar", "Cherry", "Oak"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1948", "Over $1.2 million in molding and stair-part inventory", "Custom knife library for one-of-a-kind profiles", "Historic renovation portfolio including Utah State Capitol and Governor\u2019s Mansion", "Nationwide shipping from Utah facility"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1948 by Alfred Huetter -> /about-us", "Family-owned since founding -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Murray, Utah -> db, /about-us", "Manufactures custom millwork, stair parts, moldings, cabinetry -> /about-us, /", "Inventory over $1.2 million -> /about-us", "Projects include Governor''s Mansion, Utah State Capitol, The Children''s Center, O.C. Tanner renovations -> /about-us", "Materials: alder, knotty alder, maple, poplar, cherry, oak -> /about-us", "Purpose: provide financially sound company for wholesale millwork... -> /about-us", "Motto: Quality and Craftsmanship live in our Name -> /about-us", "Custom knife inventory for unique profiles -> /about-us", "Historic renovation capabilities -> /about-us", "Nationwide shipping ->