UPDATE companies SET description='Hunt & Noyer Furniture was founded in 2013 in the Village of Clarkston, Michigan. The company takes its name from the surnames of founder Kyle’s parents, DesNoyer and Huntoon, honoring a Midwestern family lineage of generations of hardworking craftsmen. The small business began with a commitment to tradition and the belief that quality furniture should be passed down.

The workshop designs and handcrafts a range of furniture including benches, dining tables, consoles, cabinets, seating, and upholstered pieces, with a specialty in walnut. Beyond its standard collection, the company accepts custom one‑off commissions for private homes as well as large‑scale public and corporate projects. It also partners with interior designers, offering a trade discount on current collection items. Production is described as thoughtfully designed and built for generations, though facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

Hunt & Noyer serves residential clients, interior designers, and commercial and public‑sector customers. Examples from the company’s site include custom dining tables for a homeowner in Northville, a Solomon Upholstered Bench for a client in Washington, D.C., a custom crib for a nursery in Jackson, and corporate or public installations. The company welcomes studio visits for quotes and collaboration.

The founders say they are driven by a love of modernism and a desire to create heirloom pieces, emphasizing that trends change but quality is timeless. They describe their work as coming from the soul, with a passion for design, a commitment to craft, and respect for the legacy of furniture makers in their family.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted furniture manufacturing", "Cabinet making", "Seating fabrication", "Table manufacturing", "Bench manufacturing", "Upholstery", "Walnut woodworking", "Custom commissions", "Interior design collaboration"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Public sector", "Interior design"], "materials": ["Walnut"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom one\u2011off commissions and large\u2011scale public/corporate projects", "Trade discount for interior designers", "Heirloom\u2011quality pieces designed for generations", "Handcrafted in Michigan using handpicked walnut", "Family legacy of Midwestern craftsmanship"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2013 -> db", "Headquarters Village of Clarkston, Michigan -> db", "Founder Kyle (DesNoyer and Huntoon family names) -> homepage", "Handcrafted furniture in Michigan -> homepage", "Custom one-off commissions and large-scale projects -> homepage", "Trade discount for interior designers -> homepage", "Walnut wood specialty -> homepage", "Family legacy of craftsmanship -> homepage", "Products: benches, tables, consoles, cabinets, seating -> homepage and capabilities", "Serves residential, commercial, public, interior designers -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We take on everything from custom one-off commissions for private homes to large scale public and corporate projects.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hunt-noyer-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ICON Injection Molding, Inc. was founded in 2001 in Phoenix, Arizona, by three brothers—Danny, Philip, and Steve Kleitsch. The brothers had worked in their father’s injection molding and tooling shop since the late 1970s, learning the craft of fine tool building and customer relationships. After their father sold the business, they launched their own family-owned and operated company, naming it ICON after becoming the first custom molder in Arizona to adopt electric-hybrid molding machines.

The company provides custom plastic injection molding solutions, including tooling, machining, assembly, and secondary operations. Its facility houses 42 presses ranging from 15 to 720 tons, with capabilities for clean room molding, overmolding, rotary (vertical) molding, and scientific molding supported by automation. A quality lab equipped with Keyence 3-D inspection enables tolerances as tight as 0.00008 inch, and the team conducts capability studies (CPK), Gage R&R, first article inspections, and IQ/OQ/PQ validations.

ICON serves global markets through both domestic production and offshore strategic partnerships, offering customers the choice of “Made in USA” parts or cost-effective international sourcing. Its customers include original equipment manufacturers and supply chain partners who value responsiveness and flexibility, as noted in testimonials describing ICON as an extension of their manufacturing teams.

The company’s differentiation rests on a scientific, engineering-based approach that emphasizes problem prevention over detection. With over 100 combined years of industry experience among the Kleitsch family and staff, ICON maintains ISO 9001:2015 certification and a commitment to “Excellence from Art to Part,” delivering stable processes, low scrap rates, and quality documentation.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic Injection Molding", "Tooling & Machining", "Secondary Operations", "Clean Room Molding", "Overmolding", "Rotary (Vertical) Molding", "Scientific Molding", "Automation Capabilities", "Custom Packaging", "Capability Studies (CPK)", "Gage R&R", "First Article Inspection", "X-Bar and R Charting", "Pareto Charting", "IQ/OQ/PQ Validation", "Keyence 3-D Inspection", "Global Capabilities (Domestic & Offshore)"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["42 Injection Molding Presses (15\u2013720 tons)", "Keyence 3-D Inspection System", "Electric-Hybrid Molding Machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Keyence 3-D inspection up to .00008 tolerance", "built_on": ["Scientific, engineering-based approach to design, qualification, and manufacturing", "Family-owned with over 100 combined years of industry experience", "42 injection molding presses (15\u2013720 tons) with clean room, overmolding, and rotary molding capabilities", "In-house tooling, machining, and a quality lab with Keyence 3-D inspection to 0.00008 inch", "Global capabilities via domestic and offshore strategic partnerships"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 by Danny, Philip, and Steve Kleitsch -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us", "Located in Phoenix, Arizona -> /", "42 presses ranging from 15 to 720 tons -> /services", "Clean room molding, overmolding, rotary (vertical) molding -> /services", "Scientific molding approach -> /services", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about-us", "Keyence 3-D inspection up to .00008 tolerance -> /services", "Capability studies (CPK), Gage R&R, First Article, IQ/OQ/PQ -> /services", "Global capabilities with domestic and offshore strategic partnerships -> /services", "Over 100 combined years of industry experience -> /about-us", "Electric-hybrid molding machines (first in Arizona) -> /about-us", "Motto: Excellence from Art to Part -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "ICON Injection Molding is a family-owned and operated manufacturing company dedicated to providing products and services that exceed the expectations of our customers.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='icon-injection-molding-inc-shipping-receiving' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='IEG Plastics was founded in 2004 in Bellefontaine, Ohio. The company supplies plastic parts and assemblies to the automotive and consumer goods sectors.

The shop provides plastic injection molding, mold building, and product design services under one roof. Its capabilities include tight-tolerance molding to ±0.02 mm, insert and overmolding, robotics, sonic welding, and assembly. The facility runs RJG process control and operates an environmentally controlled metrology lab equipped with a Brown & Sharpe CMM, Micro-VU Vertex 311HC, Zeiss 3D light scanner, and Tenney environmental chamber. Mold building capacity reaches 20,000 lb tools, supported by a U.S.-based repair and engineering-change shop.

Primary markets are automotive safety components, precision consumer goods, and sporting goods. The company cites experience with high-volume, tight-tolerance parts for automotive safety devices and consumer products.

IEG Plastics emphasizes turnkey solutions that combine design, tooling, and production to reduce supply-chain complexity. Its quality system follows ISO 9001:2015 with APQP and PPAP expertise, and the firm highlights short lead times, in-house mold support, and value-added assembly as differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Mold design and building", "Engineering and product design", "DFM analysis", "Moldflow analysis", "Prototyping", "3D printing", "Low-volume functional parts", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Robotics", "Assembly", "Sonic welding", "Statistical process control (SPC)", "PPAP support", "GR&R analysis", "Gage calibration", "RJG process control", "Tight tolerance molding (\u00b10.02 mm)", "Mold repair", "Engineering changes", "Mold building up to 20,000 lbs"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Consumer goods", "Sporting goods"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["RJG process control sensors", "Brown & Sharpe CMM", "Micro-VU Vertex 311HC", "Zeiss 3D light scanner", "Tenney environmental test chamber", "Force gage", "Profilometer", "Blue light scanner", "Checking fixtures"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.02 mm (\u00b10.000787 in)", "built_on": ["Turnkey design, tooling, and production under one roof", "In-house mold building and repair with U.S. support shop", "Tight-tolerance molding to \u00b10.02 mm with RJG process control", "Advanced metrology including CMM, Micro-VU, and 3D light scanning", "Value-added assembly and secondary operations"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2004, headquartered Bellefontaine, Ohio -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /about-us, /capabilities, /quality", "Plastic injection molding, mold building, engineering/product design, assembly -> /capabilities", "Tight tolerance molding \u00b10.02 mm -> /capabilities, /quality", "Industries: automotive, consumer goods, sporting goods -> /capabilities", "Equipment: RJG Process Control, B