UPDATE companies SET description='Imricor Medical Systems was co-founded by Steve Wedan in 2006 and established in the Twin Cities area, with its headquarters in Burnsville, Minnesota. The company began with Wedan and three other pioneers aiming to bring interventional magnetic resonance (iMR) technology to the catheter ablation market. It is publicly traded on the Australian Securities Exchange (ASX:IMR).

The company develops and manufactures MR-compatible products for interventional MR procedures, including capital equipment such as the NorthStar Mapping System and the Advantage-MR EP Recorder/Stimulator, as well as single-use devices like the Vision-MR Ablation Catheter 2.0, Vision-MR Diagnostic Catheter, and steerable sheaths. Operations are based in a Burnsville facility housing research, development, quality, and commercial teams.

Imricor serves the cardiac ablation, electrophysiology, and interventional cardiology markets, supplying hospitals and cardiac centers worldwide. Early commercial customers include Dresden Heart Centre in Germany, Rady Children''s Hospital in San Diego, Amsterdam UMC, Lausanne University Hospital in Switzerland, and Haga Hospital in the Netherlands. Distribution partnerships extend to Philips, GE HealthCare, and Regional Health Care Group for Australia and New Zealand.

The company was founded to replace x-ray fluoroscopy with real-time MR guidance during cardiac ablation, leveraging MRI''s superior soft-tissue imaging to improve procedural safety and efficacy. Its stated mission remains the improvement of ablation therapy for patients globally, supported by CE Mark approvals in Europe, TGA approval in Australia, and FDA clearance for select products in the United States.', certifications=ARRAY['CE Mark','TGA Approval']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["MR-compatible medical device development", "Interventional MR catheter ablation systems", "Capital equipment manufacturing", "Single-use catheter manufacturing", "Electrophysiology recording and stimulation systems", "3D cardiac mapping systems", "Diagnostic catheter manufacturing", "Steerable sheath manufacturing", "Clinical trial management", "Regulatory compliance (CE Mark, FDA 510(k), TGA)", "Quality management system (CAPA, audit, document control, change control, training)"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Cardiac ablation", "Interventional cardiology", "Electrophysiology", "Interventional magnetic resonance (iMR)", "Pediatric cardiology"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["NorthStar Mapping System", "Advantage-MR EP Recorder/Stimulator", "Vision-MR Ablation Catheter 2.0", "Vision-MR Diagnostic Catheter", "Steerable sheaths"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First and only commercially viable iCMR ablation catheter system", "Real-time MR guidance replacing x-ray fluoroscopy for cardiac ablation", "CE Mark approved Vision-MR Ablation Catheter and Advantage-MR EP Recorder/Stimulator", "FDA cleared NorthStar Mapping System and Vision-MR Diagnostic Catheter", "Strategic partnerships with Philips and GE HealthCare for iCMR lab integration"], "facts_used": ["Co-founded by Steve Wedan in 2006 -> about-us", "Headquarters in Burnsville, Minnesota -> db", "First and only commercially viable iCMR products for catheter ablation -> about-us", "Products: NorthStar Mapping System, Advantage-MR EP Recorder/Stimulator, Vision-MR Ablation Catheter 2.0, Vision-MR Diagnostic Catheter, steerable sheaths -> about", "CE Mark approvals for Vision-MR Ablation Catheter and Advantage-MR EP Recorder/Stimulator -> about-us", "FDA clearance for NorthStar and Vision-MR Diagnostic Catheter -> about", "Commercial customers: Dresden Heart Centre, Rady Children''s Hospital, Amsterdam UMC, Lausanne University Hospital, Haga Hospital -> home, about-us", "Partnerships with Philips, GE HealthCare, Regional Health Care Group -> home, about-us", "Publicly traded on ASX (ASX:IMR) -> about", "Quality system functions: CAPA, Nonconformance Management, Audits, Document Control, Change Control, Training -> quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Imricor is a pioneer and world leader in developing MR-compatible products for interventional MR (iMR) procedures. The Company''s products include capital equipment, such as the NorthStar Mapping System and the Advantage-MR EP Recorder/Stimulator. Single-use devices include a variety of ablation catheters, diagnostic catheters, steerable sheaths, and other tools used in an iMR lab.", "founded_year": "2006", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='imricor-medical-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Imtron Electronics, based in Eden Prairie, Minnesota, has been supplying electronic components since its founding in 1988. The company operates as a stocking distributor and is led by President and General Manager Jeff Spaeth alongside a small team of sales and operations professionals.

The distributor stocks a range of connectors, crystals, thermal-management products, and power supplies from partners such as LEMO, Magtech, TXC, Henkel, and Mornsun. Imtron maintains inventory to serve global customers and emphasizes a consultative approach to help engineers select components for applications where failure is not an option.

Its customer base spans the automotive, aviation, medical, and military sectors. The company’s blog and marketing materials highlight work with medical-grade electronics manufacturers and defense programs that require rugged, compliant components.

